# Candidate: one consistent rankings snapshot, shared declared-value domain rules

## Decision

Expose GET /rankings returning all four top-ten boards, rendered through a SvelteKit /rankings server load. Four boards are at most forty compact entries: preloading them makes the approved wheel respond immediately and avoids loading/error races during its animation. Selection is local page state, optionally reflected in a same-origin URL query for reload/share behavior; it never calls the Rust API from the browser. The landing link navigates to this real route.

Prefer a fixed-cost batched source read plus domain aggregation for this first implementation. Do not call EntityDetailsService::member for each MP or funder_funding for each funder. Those paths pull unnecessary history and alias evidence and generate N+1 queries. Do not duplicate the financial rules in a new SQL SUM(CASE...) expression.

## Financial owner and types

Move the existing PeriodAggregate and CurrentParliamentStart out of domain/services/entity_details.rs into a domain module such as domain/models/declared_totals.rs, then have the existing member summary and rankings both use it. Preserve existing serialized member responses. In particular, an empty declaration increments declaration_count but does not create a missing funding entry or mark incomplete.

Suggested API:

```rust
pub struct CurrentParliamentStart(DateTime<Utc>);
impl CurrentParliamentStart {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn instant(&self) -> DateTime<Utc>;
    pub fn includes(&self, registered_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>) -> bool;
}
pub struct PeriodAggregate { /* current implementation */ }
impl PeriodAggregate {
    pub fn observe(&mut self, declaration: &MemberDeclaration);
    pub fn gbp_total(&self) -> DeclaredGbpPeriodTotal;
    // Existing summary currency/count accessors and finish.
}
```

The service passes boundary.instant() into the repository query. The repository applies that supplied cutoff, without owning another date literal. All current-term rows are inclusive of the cutoff; undated rows are excluded. Existing summary history/year behavior remains unchanged. GBP totals remain optional exact BigDecimal; known foreign currencies do not create incomplete GBP totals, unknown currency and missing GBP amounts do. All category IDs, including unknown ones, contribute to the MP board.

Use the existing DeclarationCategory::DonationSupport in domain logic, never a second list or category name match. Individual/company and party boards include that category's donations, loans and other support. Parties group by the recipient MP's latest stored party, not funder legal kind or direct party donations. A party is not a funder.

Suggested ranking output domain:

```rust
pub struct Rankings {
    pub current_term_start: DateTime<Utc>,
    pub members: Vec<RankingEntry<MemberRankingIdentity>>,
    pub individuals: Vec<RankingEntry<FunderRankingIdentity>>,
    pub companies: Vec<RankingEntry<FunderRankingIdentity>>,
    pub parties: Vec<RankingEntry<PartyRankingIdentity>>,
}
pub struct RankingEntry<I> {
    pub identity: I,
    pub total: DeclaredGbpPeriodTotal,
}
pub struct MemberRankingIdentity { pub id: MemberId, pub name: String }
pub struct FunderRankingIdentity { pub id: FunderId, pub name: String }
pub struct PartyRankingIdentity { pub id: PartyId, pub name: String }
pub struct PartyId(i32);
```

Avoid a loose identity object with optional member/funder/party IDs. The fixed four fields establish board completeness, and generic entry types prevent a party row with a funder ID. Introduce canonical RankingCategory only if category parsing/encoding is actually needed; do not add unused backend vocabulary solely to mirror UI state.

Sort exact optional decimal amounts descending, null last, then stable ID (and name if useful). Truncate after aggregation, not before. Keep negative and zero totals valid; never coerce absent values to zero. Preserve incomplete and declaration_count on the wire. Population of the MP board (current Commons members versus everyone with current-term declarations) must be confirmed against the approved requirement; don't silently infer current membership from registration dates. Prefer current Commons if the approved label explicitly means sitting MPs, otherwise all stored member identities with qualifying declarations.

## Repository read shape

Add domain/repositories/rankings.rs with RankingsRepo::read_current_term(start: CurrentParliamentStart) -> Result<RankingSources, RankingsRepoError>. Add domain/services/rankings.rs implementing RankingsService::rankings() -> Result<Rankings, RankingsError>, and outbound/rankings.rs for SQLx macro queries.

Use one ordered SQLx query for declarations and funding occurrences, with LEFT JOIN funding_entries to preserve declarations without entries. Select only member profile identifiers/names/latest party, declaration source ID/category ID/name/registration timestamp, funding entry ID/amount/normalized currency, and canonical funder identity/name/kind. Resolve canonical ID using COALESCE(funder_alias_groups.group_id, funder.id); join that canonical funder and funder_group_names for kind/preferred name. Never join alias text rows or family links: they multiply funding occurrences. Groups use the canonical kind, matching existing funder detail behavior. Company means exactly FunderKind::Company; Individual means exactly FunderKind::Individual. Parse persisted kind using the existing FromStr, rejecting malformed values and mapping absent kind to NotSpecified.

Factor the existing CURRENCY_WHITESPACE constant/normalization support into an outbound shared module, so new rankings and entity detail cannot disagree on blank currencies. Preserve the existing currency semantics rather than introducing uppercasing.

Reconstruct declarations using source ID, retaining entry ID to distinguish an empty left join from a real null-amount occurrence. Build lightweight per-declaration sources carrying typed canonical funder references. Feed each full declaration into its MP PeriodAggregate. For DonationSupport, feed it into its recipient-party aggregate once. Partition its occurrences by canonical funder ID and feed each funder-specific declaration once; multiple aliases in the same declaration then preserve all entries but count that declaration once for their shared canonical funder. Unnamed funding entries still count for MP and party totals, and cannot invent a funder.

A single read has one PostgreSQL statement snapshot; if profiles are read in a second fixed batch, use the repository's existing REPEATABLE READ, READ ONLY transaction pattern. Queries use sqlx::query!/query_as! with offline metadata refreshed against the actual schema. Do not embed ranking logic in handlers.

This approach is O(current-term funding occurrences) per snapshot and avoids N+1, SQL monetary rule duplication and loading alias evidence. Its scaling risk is repeated large scans; measure the actual result count and EXPLAIN plan. If insufficient, introduce compact per-declaration/currency aggregate input to the shared accumulator in a later measured change, or cache complete snapshots. Do not prematurely materialize and migrate a new rankings table.

## Transport and frontend

Add a normal handler/service dependency through the existing AppState and routes. Handler response converts each BigDecimal to normalized().to_plain_string(), exactly as entity_details does. Keep public errors generic and diagnostics server-side.

frontend/src/lib/server/rankings.ts fetches the single endpoint using supplied fetch/origin/signal, validates unknown JSON and returns a serializable model. Validate all four boards, count bounds, maximum ten entries, correct identity types, boolean incomplete, mandatory timestamp and decimal string-or-null amounts. Reject numeric amounts rather than coercing them. Reuse/extract small response parsers if doing so removes meaningful duplication; avoid a new parsing framework. Do not recalculate totals or sort financial strings in JavaScript.

frontend/src/routes/rankings/+page.server.ts owns API access. The page/feature owns URLs, display labels, formatPounds, wheel selection and any analytics. Party rows remain non-links unless a real supported party route exists. Member and canonical funder rows link to their detail routes. Error and empty states use existing MessageState/Notice patterns with only necessary copy.

## Presentation and accessibility

Keep the approved compact wheel above a top-ten list within the existing 800px content column, heading capped at 38px. Wheel controls are four native buttons in a labelled group, with aria-pressed (or proper tabs only if implementing the full tabs keyboard contract). Use category accent border plus tinted surface and a visible check/position marker for the selected control. MP purple, individuals/companies funder teal; party palette must follow the approved treatment. Focus tokens remain neutral. Icons decorative.

Add reusable UI components only for the two missing presentation patterns: CategoryWheel accepting typed options, selected ID and callback; RankingList accepting already formatted row models and optional caller-supplied identity links/snippets. UI components never format money, choose URLs or emit analytics. Export from barrel, document, and add a gallery example. Existing ResultRow/amount styles may make a dedicated RankingList unnecessary; prefer that composition if it reproduces the approved layout cleanly.

Animate list appearance on category change with keyed rows and short opacity/translate transitions. Render all final names and exact amounts immediately in DOM; do not count up money through Number, change ranking order during animation, or delay accessibility access. Respect prefers-reduced-motion with zero movement/stagger. Keep focus on the selected wheel control. No Replay, Show more, All records, redundant subsection titles, helper paragraphs or new decorative badges. Use only required declared-amount/coverage wording.

## Alternatives rejected and verification

Category-specific API requests add latency and loading-state complexity for forty total records; four all-history detail calls per row are dramatically worse. Fully SQL-owned financial totals copy the current domain rules and create regression risk. Generic arbitrary categories/periods/limits expand the scope beyond the approved four current-term boards.

Tests must prove rankings member totals equal the existing member summary current-term totals on shared fixtures, including unknown categories, empty declarations, precise huge decimals, zero, negative, absent amount, unknown/foreign currency and cutoff boundaries. Repository tests cover canonical alias consolidation, no multiplicative joins, strict kinds, party latest affiliation and distinct declaration counts. Frontend parsing tests reject malformed money and IDs; Playwright covers the landing link, each wheel category, exact displayed amount, links, empty/error states, noncolor selection, keyboard and reduced-motion behavior. Complete repository checks, frontend check/build and affected Playwright runs; capture desktop screenshots from the actual branch for PR attachments.
